    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "IL-6 inhibitors (tocilizumab, sarilumab) work in patients with an incomplete response to other biologics, alone or with methotrexate or another conventional DMARD."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Abatacept (CTLA-4 fusion protein) is indicated after an inadequate response to other DMARDs."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rituximab (anti-CD20, depletes B cells) is for refractory RA; response is often delayed but may last 6 months. Mild infusion reactions are common; rare PML and hepatitis B reactivation."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
